{
  "id": "flash-range",
  "type": "basic",
  "mode": "photo",
  "title": "Flash range and guide numbers",
  "summary": "How far a flash reaches, and what changes it.",
  "tags": [
    "flash",
    "guide number",
    "speedlite"
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "A flash's **guide number** (GN) is its power: distance in metres × aperture, at ISO 100. Divide it by your aperture to get how far it lights a subject properly."
    },
    {
      "t": "table",
      "head": [
        "Aperture",
        "GN 12 (built-in)",
        "GN 40 (speedlite)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "f/2.8",
          "4.3 m",
          "14 m"
        ],
        [
          "f/4",
          "3 m",
          "10 m"
        ],
        [
          "f/5.6",
          "2.1 m",
          "7 m"
        ],
        [
          "f/8",
          "1.5 m",
          "5 m"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "table",
      "head": [
        "Change",
        "Reach"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "ISO doubled (100 → 200)",
          "× 1.4"
        ],
        [
          "ISO × 4 (100 → 400)",
          "× 2"
        ],
        [
          "Flash head zoomed in",
          "Further, narrower beam"
        ],
        [
          "High-speed sync (HSS)",
          "Much less, often under half"
        ],
        [
          "Bounced off a ceiling",
          "Much less: about 2–3 stops lost"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "note",
      "tone": "warn",
      "text": "Above the camera's **sync speed** (about 1/200 s) normal flash leaves a dark band in the frame. Use HSS, or slow the shutter."
    },
    {
      "t": "tips",
      "items": [
        "The shutter speed barely changes flash brightness; it changes how bright the **background** is.",
        "Guide numbers on the box are often for the longest zoom setting. Wide zoom means less reach."
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "tool",
      "tool": "flash",
      "text": "Work out your flash's reach"
    },
    {
      "t": "link",
      "id": "bounce-flash",
      "text": "Guide: bounce flash"
    }
  ]
}
